bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    strict_vulkan_ganesh_refuse_dash_runs_2026-11-27, 0, "Strict Vulkan (_engine2d_draw_ir_strict_vulkan_primitive_reason, src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/engine2d/draw_ir_adv.spl:2105) and upstream Ganesh (src/lib/skia/backend/upstream_ganesh_vulkan/provider.spl:131 and :301) refuse Chrome-exact dashed border sides: since work/webrender-csslayout-20261127 (5a50573447b) a dashed side is ONE Draw IR rect carrying the dash-runs style key, whose coverage-alpha end pixels are translucent, and both lanes admit only style-free (strict Vulkan and Ganesh v2: opaque) rects. Base f43f68c218e emitted whole-px opaque dash rects they could accept. Accepted for now (option A): no current caller (vulkan_2d_qualification, wm_compare strict_semantic producers, ui_showcase host_2d_vulkan) has a straight dashed side. Fix (option C): teach both lanes to accept dash-runs (per-run fills, translucent ends blended) with device readback + RenderDoc evidence matching cpu_simd."
    strict_vulkan_ganesh_refuse_dash_runs_2026-11-27, 1, "Implemented shared draw_ir_parse_dash_runs in src/lib/common/ui/draw_ir.spl and admitted valid non-first dash-runs rects (including translucent AA end pixels) in strict Vulkan preflight/execution (src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/engine2d/draw_ir_adv.spl) and upstream Ganesh V1/V2/V3 admission and binary payload emission (src/lib/skia/backend/upstream_ganesh_vulkan/provider.spl). Verified cpu_simd parity and admission/rejection boundaries via test/01_unit/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/engine2d/strict_vulkan_dash_runs_spec.spl (4/4), test/01_unit/lib/skia/upstream_ganesh_vulkan_dash_runs_spec.spl (4/4), and test/01_unit/lib/skia/upstream_ganesh_vulkan_affine_v3_candidate_spec.spl (4/4). Headless Windows VM lacks physical Vulkan device (vkEnumeratePhysicalDevices count=0: VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED -3); physical Vulkan device readback and RenderDoc verification remain pending."

